		<section label="Stuck" sticky collapsible dividing id="variations-stuck">
			<example>
				<html>
					<p slot="description">A table can scroll horizontally, with its head, foot, first or last column staying stuck (<code>stuck</code>).</p>
					<p slot="description">You can freely stick any combination like <code>stuck="head first"</code>, <code>"foot first last"</code>, <code>"head foot first"</code>, <code>"first last"</code>, etc.</p>
					<ui-message slot="description" state="info" size="small">A stuck table possibly needs to be wrapped into an overflowing container like a <a href="/components/ui/ui-container.html">scrolling container</a> or <a href="/components/ui/ui-segment.html">scrolling segment</a>. If you don't want an extra wrapper, use <code>overflowing</code> on the table; this only works if the table's columns exceed the available width.</ui-message>
